## Web Application (apps/web) – In Accordance with Your Rules

• No changes to the philosophy: Next.js App Router + BFF (route handlers), RQ, Zod, Sentry, Lighthouse.
• **Shared packages**: `packages/api-sdk`, `packages/theme`, `packages/ui`, `packages/config`, `packages/i18n`.

-----

## Shared Packages

### packages/api-sdk

• **Source of contracts**: Backend's OpenAPI spec.
• **Generator** (e.g., `openapi-typescript`, `orval`, `openapi-generator`) → TS SDK + Zod (if the tool supports it).
• Exports Zod schemas, types, and shared JSON:API mappers.

### packages/theme

• **Design tokens** (colors, spacing, typography, radius, shadow, z-index).
• **Web**: build to CSS variables. **Mobile**: TS helpers for React Native.

### packages/ui

• **Headless primitives** (Button, Input, Select, List, Dialog).
• **Adapters**: `ui-web`, `ui-native` (composed on top of headless components).
• **Rule of Three** – extract only after 2–3 uses.

### packages/config

• **Zod schema for ENV variables**.
• **Web**: `process.env.*` (public/private via Next.js).
• **Mobile**: `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` and `Constants.expoConfig?.extra`/`process.env` (Expo).

**Example:**

```typescript
// packages/config/src/env.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const EnvSchema = z.object({
  API_URL: z.string().url(),
  SENTRY_DSN: z.string().url().optional(),
  FEATURE_X_ENABLED: z.coerce.boolean().default(false),
});

export type Env = z.infer<typeof EnvSchema>;
```

### packages/i18n

• Shared namespaces, ICU message format, initialization, and hooks.
• Mobile and web load the same resources (using a platform-specific loader).

