## CI/CD (summary)

• **Turborepo**:
• `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm e2e` (matrix: web/mobile).
• **Web**:
• Lint + typecheck + test + build + Lighthouse CI (budgets, score ≥90).
• **Mobile**:
• Lint + typecheck + unit/comp test + EAS Build (pr/preview, staging, prod).
• Maestro E2E on an emulator (PKCE login, list, detail, mutation, offline→online).
• **Security & maintenance**:
• `pnpm audit`, SAST, Renovate/Dependabot, cache `node_modules` and SDK generator artifacts.

-----

## Tests

• **Unit**: utils, use-cases, JSON:API ↔ domain mappers.
• **Component**:
• **Web**: React Testing Library + MSW.
• **Mobile**: React Native Testing Library; mock network (`whatwg-fetch`/msw/native).
• **E2E**:
• **Web**: Playwright (critical paths).
• **Mobile**: Maestro (PKCE login, critical flows, offline scenarios).
• **Contract**: schema-drift detection (Zod vs OpenAPI) in `packages/api-sdk`.

-----

## Security (shared)

• **Session/Auth**:
• **Web**: HttpOnly cookies via BFF (as before).
• **Mobile**: PKCE, secure storage, no cookies.
• **CSP/HSTS/Headers** (web), pinning/CT (mobile – backend responsibility).
• No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` (web) without sanitization.
• `Idempotency-Key` and retry policies consistent with the backend.

-----

## Definition of Done (monorepo)

• **SRP + Rule of Three applied**; no boundary violations (checked by lint boundaries/import conventions).
• **TS types + runtime validation (Zod)** at I/O boundaries.
• **Loading/Error/Empty states** are present; `ErrorBoundary` works (web + mobile).
• **A11y**: web (eslint-a11y, axe), mobile (TalkBack/VoiceOver, dynamic type).
• **Tests**:
• **Web**: unit/integration + E2E smoke tests are green.
• **Mobile**: unit/comp + E2E (Maestro) smoke tests are green.
• **OpenAPI/Zod contract has no drift**.
• **Budgets met**: web bundle + mobile JS bundle, Lighthouse ≥90.
• **Security**: PKCE + SecureStore (mobile), HttpOnly cookies (web), no secrets in the client.
• **Sentry configured** with release tracking and `requestId`.
• **ADR added** for non-trivial decisions; PR includes context/rollback plan.
• **Mobile does not depend on the web BFF** (it hits the gateway/public API directly).

-----

## Migration/Extension Policy

• **New feature**: Start with an ADR + API contract (OpenAPI/Zod), then create a skeleton in `features/<name>`.
• **Extraction** to `packages/ui` after the third use.
• **Breaking changes**: version endpoints (`/v2/*`), roll out using feature flags + OTA channels.
• **Shared abstractions**: only if reuse is proven across both web and mobile.

