## Compliance with Backend Rules (Laravel DDD)

• **JSON:API** – mapping is done on the client, without bypassing the domain.
• **Enums/statuses** – represented as string literal unions in TS.
• **Idempotency and retry** policies are aligned with the backend.
• **Dates** are in UTC (ISO 8601), presented in the user's timezone.
• **Domain errors** → friendly UI messages (`422` for forms, `409` for conflicts, `401`/`403` for auth).

-----

## Final Remarks

• The mobile app is a **first-class client** – it uses the same contracts as the web app but with a different security layer (PKCE, Secure Store, OTA, offline-first).
• **No dependency from the mobile app to the web BFF**.
• All deviations must be documented in an **ADR** in `tools/adr/`.